# The old address, for one release (JON-807; removed in the release after v0.45): bedrock-now.localhost, its subdomains
# (chat. admin. files. code. terminal. git.) and bedrock-now-preview.localhost answer with a 308 to the same path and
# query on the new name (PORTAL_HOST / PREVIEW_DOMAIN, on the port the portal is published on). Imported by Caddyfile
# with one line. Nothing here is proxied, so nothing reaches the portal or an app from these names.
#   - 308 (not 301/302) keeps the method and the body: a script's POST, PUT or DELETE is sent on to the new address
#     whole. Whether the new address accepts it is its own business: the portal never accepts the old origin as the
#     Origin of a state-changing request (it knows only its own PORTAL_ORIGIN).
#   - A WebSocket upgrade is refused (426), never redirected: the page that is redirected opens its sockets on the new
#     origin.
#   - No cookie is set, and none is passed on: these names set nothing.
# The names written here are the ones the migration (lib/migrate.sh) moves away from: docs/internal-names.md.
(legacy_redirect) {
	route {
		header -Set-Cookie
		@legacy_ws header_regexp legacy_ws Upgrade (?i)^websocket$
		header @legacy_ws X-Bn-Refused "old address: no WebSocket here"
		respond @legacy_ws "DevOS ADE moved to a new address: open it there, its sockets are opened on the new address" 426
		{block}
	}
}

http://bedrock-now.localhost {
	import legacy_redirect {
		redir http://{$PORTAL_HOST}:{$PORTAL_PORT:80}{uri} 308
	}
}

http://*.bedrock-now.localhost {
	import legacy_redirect {
		redir http://{http.request.host.labels.2}.{$PORTAL_HOST}:{$PORTAL_PORT:80}{uri} 308
	}
}

http://bedrock-now-preview.localhost, http://*.bedrock-now-preview.localhost {
	import legacy_redirect {
		redir http://{http.request.host.labels.2}.{$PREVIEW_DOMAIN:preview.invalid}:{$PORTAL_PORT:80}{uri} 308
	}
}
